2. INCIDENT CASE STUDY: CNI NETWORK FAILURE & NODE RECOVERY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[A] Symptom & Initial State:
----------------------------
When deploying nginx-deploy (5 replicas), only 3 pods scheduled on kubworker-node1 
reached Running status (3/5 Ready). Pods on kubworker-node2 remained stuck in 
ContainerCreating with <none> as their IP.

Cluster Pod Status:
NAME                          READY   STATUS              RESTARTS   AGE     IP           NODE
nginx-deploy-5dcc99ff6-5jgj4   1/1     Running             0          3m12s   10.244.1.6   kubworker-node1
nginx-deploy-5dcc99ff6-7l98k   1/1     Running             0          3m12s   10.244.1.8   kubworker-node1
nginx-deploy-5dcc99ff6-h9clr   0/1     ContainerCreating   0          3m12s   <none>       kubworker-node2
nginx-deploy-5dcc99ff6-knqzb   1/1     Running             0          3m12s   10.244.1.7   kubworker-node1
nginx-deploy-5dcc99ff6-v899g   0/1     ContainerCreating   0          3m12s   <none>       kubworker-node2


[B] Root Cause Diagnostics:
---------------------------
Step 1 - Pod Event Inspection:
Command:
  kubectl describe pod nginx-deploy-5dcc99ff6-h9clr

Error Output:
  Warning  FailedCreatePodSandbox  6m26s  kubelet
  Failed to create pod sandbox: rpc error: code = Unknown desc = failed to setup network for sandbox: 
  plugin type="flannel" failed (add): failed to load flannel 'subnet.env' file: 
  open /run/flannel/subnet.env: no such file or directory

Step 2 - CNI DaemonSet Status:
Command:
  kubectl get pods -n kube-flannel -o wide

Status Output:
  kube-flannel-ds-5fg9g   1/1   Running            3 (35h ago)     172.31.13.232   kubmaster-node
  kube-flannel-ds-7vhqk   0/1   CrashLoopBackOff   480 (41s ago)   172.31.12.72    kubworker-node2
  kube-flannel-ds-cp5vs   1/1   Running            4 (40m ago)     172.31.4.17     kubworker-node1

Step 3 - Flannel Crash Logs:
Command:
  kubectl logs -n kube-flannel kube-flannel-ds-7vhqk --previous

Root Cause Log:
  E0829 02:28:24.412497 1 main.go:292] Failed to check br_netfilter: 
  stat /proc/sys/net/bridge/bridge-nf-call-iptables: no such file or directory


[C] Permanent Remediation (Applied on kubworker-node2):
-------------------------------------------------------
1. Load the missing kernel module:
   sudo modprobe br_netfilter

2. Enable bridge filtering and IP forwarding in sysctl:
   sudo sysctl -w net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables=1
   sudo sysctl -w net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables=1
   sudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=1

3. Persist kernel module across reboots:
   cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/k8s.conf
   overlay
   br_netfilter
   EOF

4. Persist sysctl parameters across reboots:
   cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/k8s.conf
   net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables = 1
   net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables = 1
   net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1
   EOF

5. Apply all system configurations:
   sudo sysctl --system


[D] Pod Recycling & Verification (From Master Node):
----------------------------------------------------
1. Restart the failing Flannel pod:
   kubectl delete pod -n kube-flannel kube-flannel-ds-7vhqk

2. Verify all pods receive IP addresses and transition to Running:
   kubectl get pods -o wide

